1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,504
Here's a quest, and here's a boss.

2
00:00:02,954 --> 00:00:05,671
Here's a boarding party, and a ruin.

3
00:00:06,571 --> 00:00:10,817
A writer typed every one of these, in plain words, in a text file.

4
00:00:11,717 --> 00:00:14,988
And by the end of this course, that writer is you.

5
00:00:16,788 --> 00:00:18,521
Today, you type nothing.

6
00:00:19,421 --> 00:00:21,371
You play, and you watch,

7
00:00:21,821 --> 00:00:24,478
and I show you what you're going to build.

8
00:00:25,678 --> 00:00:28,199
Artemis Cosmos is a starship bridge.

9
00:00:29,099 --> 00:00:33,160
One copy of the game runs the story, and we call that the server.

10
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:35,936
Every other screen is one station:

11
00:00:36,386 --> 00:00:39,543
Helm steers, Weapons fires, Science scans,

12
00:00:39,993 --> 00:00:42,897
Comms talks, and Engineering keeps her running.

13
00:00:44,697 --> 00:00:48,552
What the crew is asked to do, who calls them, and what they find:

14
00:00:49,002 --> 00:00:51,156
all of that is a mission.

15
00:00:52,056 --> 00:00:54,482
And a mission is what you'll write.

16
00:00:55,682 --> 00:00:57,020
Start the game with me.

17
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:00,145
The first screen has the game's name,

18
00:01:00,595 --> 00:01:07,389
and three buttons at the bottom left: start server, start client, and options.

19
00:01:08,289 --> 00:01:11,984
One computer runs the game for everybody, so press start server.

20
00:01:13,784 --> 00:01:16,501
Now you choose twice.

21
00:01:17,401 --> 00:01:21,543
First, you choose a mission, and that's Legendary Missions.

22
00:01:21,993 --> 00:01:25,318
Press initialize mission, and wait a few seconds.

23
00:01:26,218 --> 00:01:29,666
Then you choose a map inside it, and that's Siege.

24
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,009
Remember those two lists,

25
00:01:33,459 --> 00:01:37,851
because in two lectures' time, there's a line in the first one that you made.

26
00:01:39,651 --> 00:01:41,491
Now press start mission.

27
00:01:42,391 --> 00:01:44,502
The server only runs the game,

28
00:01:44,952 --> 00:01:49,145
so to fly, you start the game a second time, and press start client.

29
00:01:50,045 --> 00:01:53,717
Connect to your own server, pick Helm, and press ready.

30
00:01:54,917 --> 00:01:56,801
Here's what the game has asked us to do.

31
00:01:57,701 --> 00:02:00,725
It's one job, in three parts:

32
00:02:01,175 --> 00:02:05,608
break the siege, don't lose every starbase, and mind the clock.

33
00:02:07,408 --> 00:02:10,378
Now look at this, because this is the file.

34
00:02:11,278 --> 00:02:13,644
The square brackets hold the name on the screen,

35
00:02:14,094 --> 00:02:16,876
and the last line is what the crew is told.

36
00:02:17,776 --> 00:02:20,314
Required, true, means you can't win without it.

37
00:02:22,114 --> 00:02:25,512
Nobody programmed this quest. Somebody typed it.

38
00:02:26,412 --> 00:02:30,253
And Class One ends with you having typed a chain of these.

39
00:02:31,453 --> 00:02:34,230
Now the same map, with one change.

40
00:02:35,130 --> 00:02:38,619
On the start screen, the options panel has a line called Boss,

41
00:02:39,069 --> 00:02:42,043
and I choose the Warlord.

42
00:02:43,843 --> 00:02:45,351
A boss doesn't come at the start.

43
00:02:46,251 --> 00:02:48,810
She waits until we've destroyed three raiders in every four.

44
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:52,540
Then she arrives, and a new job joins the list.

45
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,316
Now here's her file.

46
00:02:56,216 --> 00:02:59,089
Twenty-five percent means a quarter are left.

47
00:02:59,539 --> 00:03:01,971
Then two fleets, and her name and her hull.

48
00:03:02,871 --> 00:03:06,006
In Class Two, you copy this file, change the words,

49
00:03:06,456 --> 00:03:08,682
and your own boss is in that list.

50
00:03:09,882 --> 00:03:12,099
This one, you can't play today.

51
00:03:12,999 --> 00:03:16,110
It isn't in the game's menus, so just watch.

52
00:03:17,910 --> 00:03:19,608
Some of the crew leave the ship,

53
00:03:20,058 --> 00:03:22,280
and each console becomes a handheld.

54
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:26,631
There's a line of story, and the ways out, as buttons.

55
00:03:28,431 --> 00:03:30,015
Now think of two of them together.

56
00:03:30,915 --> 00:03:33,365
They're in the same room, with different choices:

57
00:03:33,815 --> 00:03:36,057
the surgeon is offered what the engineer isn't.

58
00:03:36,957 --> 00:03:40,590
It's a story told in rooms, and every reader has their own copy.

59
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:42,479
And that's Class Three.

60
00:03:43,679 --> 00:03:45,114
And then there's this.

61
00:03:46,014 --> 00:03:49,416
It's a built place, and it's old, with rooms.

62
00:03:50,316 --> 00:03:52,366
The writer didn't draw it.

63
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:56,111
The writer wrote, a room, this big, here,

64
00:03:56,561 --> 00:03:58,540
and the game put up the walls.

65
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,250
A quest leads the ship through it,

66
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,160
and a place speaks.

67
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:09,607
And for ten seconds, the story takes the main screen.

68
00:04:10,507 --> 00:04:11,949
And that's Class Four.

69
00:04:13,149 --> 00:04:15,767
So what is a mission?

70
00:04:16,667 --> 00:04:18,823
It's a folder, with seven files,

71
00:04:19,273 --> 00:04:22,328
and five of them are made for you.

72
00:04:23,228 --> 00:04:26,061
The two that matter are the fact sheet, and the story file.

73
00:04:27,861 --> 00:04:30,811
The fact sheet is every word the crew reads.

74
00:04:31,711 --> 00:04:33,570
Here's one quest: its name,

75
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:36,592
its facts between the two rows of hyphens,

76
00:04:37,042 --> 00:04:39,122
and what the crew is told.

77
00:04:40,022 --> 00:04:42,446
Done when, reach derelict five hundred.

78
00:04:42,895 --> 00:04:45,283
It means just what it says.

79
00:04:47,083 --> 00:04:50,180
The story file is short, and it comes ready-made.

80
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:55,182
Now and then, you paste a few lines into it from a card, like this one.

81
00:04:56,082 --> 00:04:59,443
It says: when the step starts, wait twenty seconds,

82
00:04:59,893 --> 00:05:02,207
bring in a tug, and tell the quests.

83
00:05:04,007 --> 00:05:06,163
You'll be able to read this by Lecture Eleven.

84
00:05:07,063 --> 00:05:09,319
And you'll never write one from a blank page.

85
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:11,988
There are six classes.

86
00:05:12,888 --> 00:05:17,310
One is your desk, and a story told in quests.

87
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:21,836
Two is people who talk, and a boss of your own.

88
00:05:22,736 --> 00:05:26,089
Then come three that you can take in any order:

89
00:05:26,539 --> 00:05:29,700
three is boarding parties, four is ruins,

90
00:05:30,150 --> 00:05:32,991
and five is a universe of your own.

91
00:05:33,891 --> 00:05:37,027
And six is twenty evenings of play in that universe.

92
00:05:38,827 --> 00:05:42,449
Some of the later lectures are still being made, and the page says which.

93
00:05:43,649 --> 00:05:45,182
So play ten minutes of Siege.

94
00:05:46,082 --> 00:05:48,325
Write down three things that happened,

95
00:05:48,775 --> 00:05:52,022
and who, or what, caused each one.

96
00:05:52,922 --> 00:05:54,571
And keep the page,

97
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:58,809
because next time, we find where all of this lives on your computer.
